.TH SDL_CloseAsyncIO 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CloseAsyncIO \- Close and free any allocated resources for an async I/O object.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_CloseAsyncIO(SDL_AsyncIO *asyncio, bool flush, SDL_AsyncIOQueue *queue, void *userdata);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Closing a file is _also_ an asynchronous task! If a write failure were to happen during the closing process, for example, the task results will report it as usual\[char46]
.PP
Closing a file that has been written to does not guarantee the data has made it to physical media; it may remain in the operating system\(aqs file cache, for later writing to disk\[char46] This means that a successfully-closed file can be lost if the system crashes or loses power in this small window\[char46] To prevent this, call this function with the
.BR flush
parameter set to true\[char46] This will make the operation take longer, and perhaps increase system load in general, but a successful result guarantees that the data has made it to physical storage\[char46] Don\(aqt use this for temporary files, caches, and unimportant data, and definitely use it for crucial irreplaceable files, like game saves\[char46]
.PP
This function guarantees that the close will happen after any other pending tasks to
.BR asyncio ,
so it\(aqs safe to open a file, start several operations, close the file immediately, then check for all results later\[char46] This function will not block until the tasks have completed\[char46]
.PP
Once this function returns true,
.BR asyncio
is no longer valid, regardless of any future outcomes\[char46] Any completed tasks might still contain this pointer in their
.BR SDL_AsyncIOOutcome
data, in case the app was using this value to track information, but it should not be used again\[char46]
.PP
If this function returns false, the close wasn\(aqt started at all, and it\(aqs safe to attempt to close again later\[char46]
.PP
An
.BR SDL_AsyncIOQueue
must be specified\[char46] The newly-created task will be added to it when it completes its work\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I asyncio
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
structure to close\[char46]
.TP
.I flush
true if data should sync to disk before the task completes\[char46]
.TP
.I queue
a queue to add the new
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
to\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
an app-defined pointer that will be provided with the task results\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread, but two threads should not attempt to close the same object\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

